@MinimalApiEntity_HostAddress = http://localhost:5295

### Pizza GETs use Redis cache-aside with a 60-second absolute TTL.
### POST invalidates the list and exact-name cache after commit. Concurrent fills/external writes can be stale until expiry.
### Missing names are not cached. Redis failures are logged and fall back to PostgreSQL.
### Reads allow 32 active + 100 queued requests per process; overflow returns 429.
### Local Redis: 127.0.0.1:56380 (development only, no auth, loopback binding).
### Start local services with scripts\Start-Postgres.ps1. Production needs a secured Redis connection and a prefix unique to its database/environment.
GET {{MinimalApiEntity_HostAddress}}/pizza
Accept: application/json

###

GET {{MinimalApiEntity_HostAddress}}/pizza/Margherita
Accept: application/json

### Unknown names return 404

GET {{MinimalApiEntity_HostAddress}}/pizza/NonexistentPizza
Accept: application/json

###

### POST: queue overflow or a 5-second database lock wait returns 429 with Retry-After.
### The queue holds at most 100 requests per API process, not 100 across all instances.
POST {{MinimalApiEntity_HostAddress}}/pizza
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Margherita",
  "description": "Tomato, mozzarella, and basil"
}

### Missing or blank names return 400

POST {{MinimalApiEntity_HostAddress}}/pizza
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": " "
}

###
